    "body": "Adding [bellini666/pytest-language-server](https://github.com/bellini666/pytest-language-server?rgh-link-date=2025-11-18T07%3A30%3A18Z)\r\n\r\nThe repository has 115 starts as of today, and a good evidence of usage across multiple stores:\r\n\r\n- 27k+ downloads on zed ([zed.dev/extensions/pytest-language-server](https://zed.dev/extensions/pytest-language-server))\r\n- 154+ installs on vscode ([marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=bellini666.pytest-language-server](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=bellini666.pytest-language-server))\r\n- 1106+ installs on jetbrains ([plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/29056-pytest-language-server](https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/29056-pytest-language-server))\r\n\r\nOf course, both vscode and jetbrains will have less usage, as pylance extends pyright with some pytest fixture LS features, and pycharm as well. But zed, like neovim, doesn't have access to any LS which would provide such a feature, so it is a lot more popular there\r\n\r\nThe project has received contributions from the community as well since I first opened [this previous PR](https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/pull/4201)",
